Backport native LLVM 22/23 support to CppInterOp 1.9.0.

Upstream: https://github.com/compiler-research/CppInterOp
Compared: v1.9.0 .. 3a6e86f13612d850d334f3b5d7094c5f8a75b02a
Adapted from:
  e1c39c911c6f0c55c6c9e55ffc69cb648373db72 (LLVM 22 native support)
  87012b46179327e7a0dd01a98a4aba5fc89e3b72 (silent error status prerequisite)
  2717d9477a33d680210ada897c07aa20da3acb94 (LLVM 23 support)
  a438c13316a8c1917cb86e00d5b0d95e6aee75f5 (static LLVM linkage)
  261bebbf25c8f709d2e2490fe6e3f876f6ec5920 (retain system dependencies)

Preserve the 1.9.0 public API and LLVM 19-21 compatibility paths.
Do not import 2.x opaque handles, Box/Result, tracing, or TableGen-generated APIs.
LLVM 23 needs the ABI component and anonymous tag printing changes.
Use the upstream silent diagnostic consumer on both LLVM 22 and 23:
LLVM 22 also crashes in CodeGen on silently parsed invalid statements
when SuppressAllDiagnostics prevents error accounting. 
Include cmath explicitly as upstream does instead of depending on transitive includes.
This backport covers the feedstock's native clang-repl configuration;
Emscripten and LLVM_BUILT_WITH_OOP_JIT are not enabled by this recipe.

